          "Maintain active relationship with Black community institutions and leadership: at 47% of the district, the Black population is the demographic foundation of the seat, but Phillips' 79% margin can mask divergence among Black voters around education quality, criminal justice reform, and economic development — active engagement with churches, civic organizations, and community leaders is essential to prevent base erosion rather than relying on inherited partisan loyalty.",
          "Address education and workforce pipeline specifics for young adults: the 45.5% college attainment and 36.5 median age signal a constituency invested in education quality and economic opportunity — student debt, higher education affordability, and the pathway from education to well-paid employment are the material concerns most likely to drive or suppress turnout among younger voters, and deserve concrete legislative attention rather than generic statements.",
