          { name: "Taking Black Voter Turnout for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "The 45.24% Black population and 82% Democratic margin together indicate that Black voter turnout and preference are the entire electoral foundation of this seat. Any incumbent who campaigns as though Black voter mobilization is automatic — rather than something that must be earned through concrete constituent service and demonstrated progress on economic issues — risks a decline in turnout or candidate preference that would rapidly erase the current margin. The 18% Republican share suggests minimal cross-over, and the 82% Democratic number is only durable if Black constituents believe they are being served." }
