          "Avoid framing racial or demographic differences as the basis for policy — the district's near-parity between Black and white populations means that any candidate who treats either community as a special interest rather than as integrated constituents with shared economic concerns is ceding the racial-coalition advantage that produced Edwards' 70% margin.",
