          "Lead on education and property tax policy with specificity: 54.7% college attainment means this constituency understands K-12 funding adequacy, school quality metrics, and property tax fairness at a sophisticated level — generic rhetoric about 'supporting schools' or 'fiscal responsibility' will not move voters who can evaluate the actual policy trade-offs.",
          "Consolidate younger renters (19.1% of district) as a swing constituency within the affluent base: housing affordability, student debt, and economic mobility are the material concerns for college-educated adults under 45, and a legislative agenda that addresses these concerns directly (not as afterthoughts) is the path to converting renters into invested constituents.",
          "Do not assume that affluence and education automatically anchor Democratic voters: college-educated suburban and exurban voters have demonstrated willingness to split their tickets and support fiscally conservative candidates when they believe their property values, schools, and quality of life are better protected by Republican governance — a 52% win on a 48% split is too narrow to treat as safe."
