          "Defend against pro-business, pro-innovation messaging from Republican challengers — the 60-40 margin in a $120K+ income district is vulnerable to a challenger who positions themselves as pro-growth and anti-regulatory bloat; Puri must reframe regulation as protecting homeowner property values, school quality, and professional standards rather as ideological overreach.",
          "Engage the 40% opposition directly on specific governance grievances — in a high-income, educated district, opposition is not purely partisan; identify whether it concentrates around tax policy, development/zoning decisions, school funding allocation, or business regulation, and offer concrete responses rather than assuming the 60% floor is stable."
