          "Consolidate white working-class homeowners on material economic security: property tax fairness, home-repair affordability, healthcare costs for households at $64,430 income, and rural or semi-rural service reliability are the direct governance concerns for a 67.81% white, 28.2% renter, 44.8-year-old median age constituency.",
          "Build authentic Black constituency engagement—the 18.82% Black population in a 53-47 district represents roughly 10-12 percentage points of the margin; any erosion in Black turnout or unity is sufficient to flip the seat, so specific agenda items on workforce development, healthcare access, and neighborhood investment are both policy obligations and electoral necessities.",
          "Do not treat the 53% result as a durable coalition—it is a narrow plurality in a swing district where renter-majority younger adults, working-class homeowners, the Black community, and the unknown 5.24% are not locked into any single candidate; consistent constituent engagement and material delivery on healthcare, housing, and economic opportunity are required to hold this seat."
