          { name: "Education Quality and School Funding", tag: "lean-into", why: "At 35% college-educated adults, this district is above the baseline but not elite—suggesting strong value placed on educational attainment as economic security. A 41.7-year median age indicates many residents have school-age children or recently launched them. School funding, curriculum quality, and education ROI resonate with a constituency that views education as essential economic infrastructure." },
          { name: "Racial Diversity and Inclusion Programs", tag: "careful", why: "The district is 85.7% White with Black residents at 4.94%, Hispanic at 3.25%, and Asian at 1.66%, leaving a 4.54% gap likely attributable to American Indian/Alaska Native populations. While diversity is present, the overwhelming White majority means messaging around racial equity or identity-specific programs risks alienating the district's demographic center without meaningfully energizing smaller constituencies. Framing inclusivity in economic or civic terms rather than identity-first language is safer territory." },
          { name: "Rent Control and Tenant Advocacy", tag: "avoid", why: "At only 20.4% renters, this district is heavily homeowner-dominant, making tenant-focused policy messaging strategically weak. Renters lack the electoral weight to drive outcomes, and heavy promotion of renter protections risks signaling hostility to landlord-owners who likely comprise 40-50% of the property-holding population. The constituency's economic interests align with property value stability, not renter regulation." },
          { name: "Demographic Change and Immigration", tag: "avoid", why: "With 85.7% White residents and a median age of 41.7, the district has limited demographic dynamism and is not experiencing rapid population turnover or immigration pressure. Messaging centered on immigration policy or demographic change lacks salience because the lived reality of the district is demographic stability. Pivoting campaign messaging around these issues signals misalignment with the district's actual conditions and wastes persuasion bandwidth." }
