          "Exploit the 39% Democratic base for turnout, not persuasion: The 61–39 result is robust but not unbreakable. Rather than pursue the unlikely conversion of property-owning Republicans, focus on maximizing turnout among the existing 39% and recruiting persuadable economic-anxiety voters under 50."
