          "Address the college-attainment gap (22%, lowest in sequence): this district's workforce is concentrated in service, manufacturing, and trades rather than knowledge economy sectors; skills training, union apprenticeships, and wage-floor policy are more relevant constituent concerns than higher education access, and candidates must speak to that material reality.",
