          "Do not take the 66% margin as permission to ignore the 34% opposition — in a district this wealthy, white, and educated, 34% Democratic support signals material dissatisfaction among the exact constituency (college-educated professionals) most likely to swing in future cycles if healthcare, education funding, or environmental concerns activate them.",
