          "Do not take the 62% for granted as a stable Republican floor — the 38% opposition in a rural, older, lower-education district typically indicates economic frustration rather than partisan conversion, making authenticity on economic security concerns the difference between holding and losing a seat that appears comfortable.",
          "Engage the small but present Native American community (~3.5%) on healthcare access and economic development with genuine specificity rather than token acknowledgment; rural healthcare and tribal healthcare systems in Michigan overlap, and a legislator who understands this intersection serves the whole district more effectively.",
          "Recognize that limited college attainment (19.3%) means this district is not responsive to credential-heavy messaging or abstract policy frameworks — speak to concrete economic pressures, real constituent experiences, and what you have actually delivered or will deliver to address them."
