          { name: "Assuming the 56% Republican Margin Is Durable Without Active Consolidation", tag: "avoid", why: "A 56-44 result in a district this demographically Republican (88.6% white, $73,703 income, 36.2% college-educated, 80% homeowners) is approximately 5-8 points weaker than the district's demographic profile predicts. This gap represents active erosion among college-educated voters, older adults, and affluent women — constituencies that have defected in significant numbers from Republican candidates nationally. Any incumbent or candidate who treats the 56% as a stable floor and campaigns accordingly will find that erosion continues rather than stabilizes. The 44% opposition is the strategic fact; understanding its sources and directly addressing them is the prerequisite for holding or winning this seat." }
